# Skip to My Lou, strum and sing (repertoire plan: skip-to-my-lou). Your part: A (x02220) and
# E7 (020100), one downstrum on every beat of 2/4. Each sung line takes two bars: A under line 1,
# E7 under line 2, A under line 3, then E7 and A under the last line. The words of each line sit
# above its first strum.
# The sung tune is not written out here: this file holds only the part the plan specifies (the
# strum and the chord rhythm) and the traditional words, so nothing in it is a guessed melody.
title: Skip to My Lou
id: skip-to-my-lou
composer: Traditional American
source: Play-party song reported in the 1840s, traditional verses; arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (traditional); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 1
tags: strumming, first chord change, a, e7, play-party, beginner
tempo: 100
time: 2/4
key: A

